# IJG and MIT Licenses

jpegtran-js combines two independent licenses. The WebAssembly module is a
build of the Independent JPEG Group's libjpeg; everything else is original
work of this project.

  - `src/jpegtran_wrapper.c`, `src/index.ts`, `src/cli.ts`, `build.sh`,
    `test.ts`, `test/simple.ts`, `test/crop.ts` and `docs/` are original
    work of this project, licensed under the MIT License — see "MIT License"
    below. They are not IJG code. (`dist/index.js`, `dist/index.d.ts` and
    `dist/cli.js` are compiled from the TypeScript sources and are covered
    by the same MIT License.)

  - `dist/jpegtran.wasm` and `dist/jpegtran.mjs` are a compiled build of the
    Independent JPEG Group's libjpeg, release 10, together with that release's
    `transupp.c` transform engine, linked against the wrapper above. They are
    covered by the IJG License — see "Independent JPEG Group (IJG) License"
    below.

Condition (1) of the IJG License requires that additions, deletions and
changes to the original files be clearly indicated. The libjpeg and transupp
sources are used unmodified; this repository adds files next to them rather
than editing them. `jpeg/` is a throwaway build copy of the libjpeg source
tree, regenerated by `build.sh` and not distributed with this repository.

